Task 2: Create and configure secure blob storage
1.Azure portal-> Storage accounts->select a storage account -> Data storage -> Containers -> Create using  
Setting | Value |
    | --- | --- |
    | Name | `data`  |
    | Public access level | Notice the access level is set to private |
2. Open the created container -> Access policy -> Add policy -> Legal hold-> Time-based retention 
 | Setting | Value |
    | --- | --- |
    | Policy type | **Time-based retention**  |
    | Set retention period for | `180` days |
3. Save
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Manage blob uploads
1.Storage account-> settings-> configuration-> Enable Allow storage account key access-> Save
2.Access Control (IAM) -> Add role assignment-> Storage Blob Data Contributor role->Assign 
3. Assign the Storage File Data Privileged Contributor role
4.Upload data to the storage container.
5. Upload blob -> Advanced
 | Setting | Value |
    | --- | --- |
    | Browse for files | add the file you have selected to upload |
    | Select **Advanced** | |
    | Blob type | **Block blob** |
    | Block size | **4 MiB** |
    | Access tier | **Hot**  (notice the other options) |
    | Upload to folder | `securitytest` |
    | Encryption scope | Use existing default container scope |
6.Upload 
7.Confrim the file was upload and the folder was created.
8.Download the uploaded file 
9.Copy and paste the uploaded file url 
10. Results: publicAccessNotPermitted and Public access is not permitted on this storage account
